# Vowels (§5 lines 1234–1241). Length is otherwise left unmarked: it is predictable from the
# spelling once the stressed final syllable's coda is known (§5 lines 1274–1281 [wiki-cy-orth
# §Predicting vowel length]). ⟨y⟩ = /ə/ in non-final syllables (§5 line 1256); /ə/ never
# reaches a final syllable here ([repair]). Final-syllable /ɪ/ is written i (i-dot, line 1266).
# The lexical n l r class is the one place a long vowel is not predictable from the spelling
# (§5 lines 1279–1281): "marked with a circumflex if long" — tâl, tôn, gêr (§4.3 line 1084).
